<title>USA: Crawford &amp; Co Q1 EPS $0.13 vs $0.20.</title>
<headline>Crawford &amp; Co Q1 EPS $0.13 vs $0.20.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>CRAWFORD &amp; COMPANY</p>
<p>		Comparative Statements of Income</p>
<p>(In Thousands of Dollars, Except Share and Per Share Data)</p>
<p>    3 mos. ended March 31	   1997	  1996  Pct. chg.</p>
<p> REVENUES				$165,951   $161,563	3</p>
<p>COSTS AND EXPENSES:</p>
<p> COST OF SERVICES		     119,594    116,804	2</p>
<p> SELLING, GENERAL AND ADMIN.	 27,075     27,281    (1)</p>
<p> RESTRUCTURING CHARGE(A)	     13,000	    0    ---</p>
<p> TOTAL COSTS AND EXPENSES	   159,669    144,085     11</p>
<p>INCOME BEFORE INCOME TAXES AND</p>
<p>  MINORITY INTEREST		     6,282     17,478   (64)</p>
<p> INCOME TAXES			     3,166	7,047   (55)</p>
<p> INCOME BEFORE MINORITY INTEREST    3,116     10,431   (70)</p>
<p> MINORITY INTEREST		    (3,199)	    0    ---</p>
<p> NET INCOME				 6,315     10,431   (39)</p>
<p> NET INCOME PER SHARE		    0.13	 0.20   (35)</p>
<p>WTD. AVG. NO. OF CLASS A AND</p>
<p>CLASS B COMMON SHARES OUTST. 50,028,197 51,465,714</p>
<p>(A) THE COMPANY RECORDED A PRETAX CHARGE OF $13 MILLION FOR PERSONNEL, FACILITIES AND OTHER COSTS ASSOCIATED WITH INTEGRATION OF THE RECENTLY ACQUIRED THOMAS HOWELL GROUP. AFTER REFLECTING INCOME TAX BENEFITS OF $4.3 MILLION AND MINORITY INTEREST SHARE OF $3.5 MILLION, THIS CHARGE REDUCED CRAWFORD'S FIRST QUARTER 1997 NET INCOME BY $5.2 MILLION, OR $0.10 PER SHARE.</p>
